Build a package from a checkout with:

    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

The build needs Go 1.26 or newer on PATH and network access to download the
Go modules (or run `go mod vendor` first). If Debian's golang-go is too old,
install a toolchain from https://go.dev/dl/ and add `-d` to skip the
build-dependency check. `DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nocheck` skips the tests.

After installing, initialise or enrol the node once by hand (see
/usr/share/doc/cheesecloth/README.md), put its settings in
/etc/cheesecloth/config.yaml, then `systemctl enable --now cheesecloth`.
